Browser-specific runtime behavior:
- Uses web-lite isometric rendering by default, including capped visible pickups, turrets, enemies, bullets, and enemy shots.
- Uses cached wall/background layers so static map geometry is not rebuilt every frame.
- Uses browser-native BGM and FX audio paths where possible to avoid pygame mixer crackle under web load.
- Stores save data through browser localStorage with a primary key, backup key, and metadata key.
- Supports diagnostic URL flags such as start, diag, scenario, biome, level, duration, and feature toggles.
- Keeps enemy projectiles disabled by default on the safest browser route unless explicitly enabled for debugging.
- Uses queued/batched timed spawns so renewed waves do not enter the simulation in one browser frame.

