Browser visible feedback changes:
List the browser feedback that can be hidden, merged, cached, skipped, or trimmed, such as visible bullets, damage text, particles, paint layer, pickup bundles, turret sprites, pulse rings, or audio.

Browser cap / cadence / fallback:
Use exact values when known. Examples: visible bullets 28, visible turrets 8, visible pickups 12, max damage texts 4, max FX particles 16, DOT/paint/spikes at 20 Hz, pulse/text at 24 Hz, pickups at 30 Hz, enemy-shot fallback while enemy shots are disabled.

Browser overflow behavior:
Choose one explicit verb: drop, merge, refresh oldest, reduce spawned count, credit directly, keep simulating while hidden, or use fallback. Do not write "optimized" without saying what happens to the excess event.

Browser player-facing copy:
State the final surface decision:
- none: effect values and visible planning are unchanged.
- tooltip only: only visual feedback changes.
- card + tooltip: browser changes a planning-relevant cap, fallback, or value.
- pause/run summary: browser hides simulated persistent state, such as turrets or saved economy state.
- QA only: relevant only to diagnostic counters and not useful to players.

Browser QA proof:
Name one URL or counter. For implemented props, include at least one of: pending_bullets, web_visible_bullets, web_visible_turrets, visible_pickups, dmg_text_count, fx_particle_count, prop_trigger_counts, fallback_trigger_count, localStorage_write_ok, or browser_gap_ms.

Browser same-as-desktop expanded example:
Original version: uses bullet_hit_event as the trigger owner and the listed proc chance, damage multiplier, cooldown, boss modifier, and hit ordering. Browser version: classification = same_as_desktop. Implementation owner = bullet_hit_event. Authoritative effect values = proc chance, damage multiplier, cooldown, and boss modifier match desktop. Visible feedback changes = damage text may merge under the browser text budget. Player copy = no card note; tooltip note only if repeated text merging confuses QA. QA proof = `?start=1&diag=1` with prop_trigger_counts and damage_done matching desktop expectations.

Browser capped expanded example:
Original version: owns, draws, and simulates every purchased turret through turret_update and saved turret state. Browser version: classification = render_capped. Implementation owner = turret_update plus lite render. Authoritative effect values = owned turret count, fire rate, target selection, and damage match desktop. Visible feedback changes = browser draws nearest 8 turrets when more are owned. Overflow behavior = hidden turrets keep simulating and firing. Player copy = tooltip or pause summary says "Browser: nearest 8 turrets drawn; all owned turrets still fire." QA proof = web_visible_turrets, simulated_turret_count, and turret_shots_fired.

