24. QA Acceptance Matrix (Per Prop Family)
24.1. Offense family
Acceptance checks:
No chain effect can recurse infinitely.
Per-hit and per-kill triggers respect throttles.
Boss damage modifiers always applied.
Browser acceptance:
Visible bullet cap does not stop simulated damage.
Pending-bullet headroom reduces spawned secondary bullets before frame stalls.
FX particle trimming never changes explosive or crit damage numbers.

24.2. Defense family
Acceptance checks:
Shield routing order matches section 8.2.
Reaction buffs trigger once per valid event and honor internal cooldown.
No reflection feedback loops.
Browser acceptance:
Shield/carapace/plating state survives browser refresh when it is part of carry/save state.
Enemy-shot-dependent reactions have an enemyshots QA route or a fallback.
Merged shield text does not hide whether mitigation happened.

24.3. Economy family
Acceptance checks:
Shop discounts and surcharges apply in fixed deterministic order.
Interest/cashback/loan logic cannot generate negative coin states.
Bandit interactions never consume charges without valid trigger.
Browser acceptance:
Visible pickup/spoil caps do not reduce credited rewards.
Loan, cashback, coupon, wanted, and protected coin counters survive localStorage reload.
If rewards are merged or credited directly, telemetry records the original earned amount and final credited amount.

24.4. Paint family
Acceptance checks:
Paint ownership and overwrite logic deterministic under simultaneous writes.
Tile caps and cleanup execute without frame spikes.
Paint effects clear correctly on level transition unless persisted by design.
Browser acceptance:
Paint state remains authoritative when paint rendering is cached, throttled, or skipped in wind/mist routes.
Paint reward props read paint_grid ownership/intensity, not rendered pixels.
Paint VFX refresh cadence does not change tick damage, slow resistance, or ownership conversion.
